## New ideas added

- **₹1,200 Water Park Ticket: What Does the Owner Keep?** — Hook: 'Ek family ne ₹1,200 ke 4 tickets liye, park owner ke paas kitna bacha?' Show the ride-and-land investment, why it only earns in 4 to 5 peak months, and how food and lockers carry the profit. Payoff: the real per-visitor margin and the footfall needed to break even. _(pattern: Rupee-per-unit breakdown of a dream-to-own business, ending in a surprising owner take-home figure (same as the petrol pump reel).; evidence: )_
- **₹3,000 MRI Scan: How Many Scans Pay for a ₹3 Crore Machine?** — Hook: 'Ek MRI machine ₹3 crore ki hai. Roz kitne scan karne padte hain tab owner ka paisa wapas aata hai?' Walk through the machine cost, running cost and daily scan capacity. Payoff: the payback in months, and why the referral cut and utilisation decide who wins. _(pattern: Big capex vs small per-unit price ('how many X to break even'), the structure of the EV charger and gym reels.; evidence: )_
- **₹250 Ka Cappuccino: Cafe Owner Ko Kitna Bachta Hai?** — Hook: 'Is ₹250 ke cup mein coffee sirf ₹20-25 ki hai, baaki paisa kahan gaya?' Split the cup into ingredient, rent, staff, royalty and profit. Payoff: the owner's real margin, and why rent and footfall matter more than the coffee. _(pattern: A familiar everyday price broken into slices with a shocking raw-cost figure, like the pizza and Zomato order reels.; evidence: )_
- **₹1 Crore Ka Flat Bika: Builder Ke Paas Kitna Bacha?** — Hook: 'Aapne ₹1 crore ka flat kharida. Builder ne usme se kitna kamaya?' Show a stacked-bar breakdown by cost bucket. Payoff: the builder's EBITDA or margin range, and how much is land versus tax versus actual construction. _(pattern: Follow ₹X of the customer's money through the chain to the owner's pocket, the same as the gas cylinder and school fee reels.; evidence: )_
- **₹5,000 Ki Flight Ticket: Airline Ko Kitna Bachta Hai?** — Hook: 'Ek flight bhar ke bhi airline ka profit sirf ₹300-400 kyun hota hai?' Slice the fare into fuel, lease, airport fees, taxes and crew. Payoff: break-even seat occupancy, and why bag fees, seat selection and food earn more than the ticket. _(pattern: Fare vs hidden costs, with a counter-intuitive twist that a full plane still doesn't mean profit (like the sleeper bus and sarkari bus contract reels).; evidence: )_
- **Railway Station Pe Chai-Snacks Stall: Licence Kaise Milta Hai Aur Kitna Kamate Hain?** — Hook: 'Platform pe ₹20 ki chai bechne ka haq kaun deta hai, aur uski licence fee kitni hai?' Explain the licence route, the licence fee as a fixed monthly cost, and the footfall versus sales maths. Payoff: monthly profit at a busy station vs a small one, and the hidden costs. _(pattern: Insider access to a licensed, hard-to-enter business ('who actually gets to run this'), like the Amul parlour and gas agency reels.; evidence: )_
